        "shortHash": "928340a",
        "hash": "928340ab4310d7d23ff6057e090a06c8b2917a56",
        "subject": "Add read-only offline support via persisted query cache",
        "body": "Add read-only offline support via persisted query cache\n\nPersist the TanStack Query cache to disk (AsyncStorage) so previously-synced\ndata renders on cold start when offline, instead of falling back to\nloading/error states. Adds a NetInfo-driven banner so users know data may be\nstale. Read-only only — no offline writes, mutation queueing, or sync.\n\n- queryPersister: AsyncStorage-backed persister (VITTIO_RQ_CACHE)\n- _layout: QueryClientProvider -> PersistQueryClientProvider; persist only\n  successful queries; mount OfflineBanner\n- queryClient: gcTime 10m -> 24h (>= persister maxAge) so restored entries\n  survive to cold start; staleTime stays 5m for prompt refetch when online\n- authStore._clearAuth: purge on-disk cache on logout so one account's data\n  can't rehydrate into the next session\n- OfflineBanner + i18n strings (en/es)\n- e2e: offline-banner.spec.ts (banner appears offline / hides online)\n\nLogout-purge cross-account isolation is verified manually on the iOS\nSimulator; no jest infra exists and bootstrapping it for one assertion isn't\nwarranted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014FCNefed5zoDxkikmJJ6D9\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1784595762000
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
